A||||7||fierosound||Just ordered BORLA EXHAUST||||10||
Z||000000||fierosound||02-18-2000||07:56 PM||||I got a call from FIERO PARTS stating they've got enough buyers to place an order with BORLA for exhaust systems (there is a minimum number of systems required, before BORLA would make a "run").  They are now requesting firm orders and payment.  I've just sent mine in.  Anyone else interested, you can still get in and order one.  Jump over to the forum below for details.  There may never be another manufacturing run on these...<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002112.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002112.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 02-19-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Carolina 88GT||02-18-2000||08:53 PM||||I got a call today as well from Tim.  Im on the band wagon with this one.||||reg||14
Z||000002||fierosound||03-06-2000||06:57 PM||||I know alot of the guys thought $420 was too expensive for a Borla stainless steel exhaust system.  Check out the price of this stainless steel exhaust system from Fiero Heaven.  <A HREF="http://www.fieroheaven.com/Exhaust.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroheaven.com/Exhaust.htm</A> <P>RS Motorsports also has a stainless steel exhaust system for US$680.  <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/</A> <P>Of course, there's always the Ocelot exhaust from The Fiero Store and GM's stock exhaust system to choose from as well.  <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/</A> <P>But at present, the Borla seems to be the best priced of the stainless steel performance exhaust systems.<p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 03-07-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||GT Bastard||03-06-2000||07:26 PM||||does he take credit cards?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||03-07-2000||12:59 PM||||GT...<P>I don't know, I sent a bank draft.  Email or phone and ask about credit cards.  If not, you can always go to your bank, and get a cash advance on your credit card with which to buy a bank money order/bank draft.  Works out the same as charging it, if that's what you wanted to do.||||reg||10
Z||000005||GT Bastard||03-08-2000||12:53 AM||||I figured if I put it on a credit card it was free.... hmmmmm....||||reg||1
Z||000006||Earne||03-08-2000||08:16 AM||||Did I understand right?  This run of the Borla's don't have the Borla tip attached.  I bought a set last year from Tim,  <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=2238074&p=17431712&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=103583&a=2238074&p=17431712&Sequence=2</A> <P>They were a little more than this price but worth it.  Are all of you reusing your stock tips?  Don't forget the Chetah pipe from the FieroStore.  It eliminates the Cat and the system sounds great that way.  Showed the car in Indiana last year at Tim's Borla stand and he sold the last six sets there.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierosound||03-09-2000||02:54 PM||||GT - your statement implied you didn't have cash, but you have a credit card.<P>Borla systems are still a go at this point.  Seems alot of "interested" parties are having a tough time getting their butts in gear to order promptly.  If the thing falls through, these will be the same people asking 3 months from now "anyone still making Borla sytems for the Fiero??" Arghhh!!! <P>See forum below:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002625.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002625.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 03-09-2000).]||||reg||1
